<section class="home-hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Self-hosted todos</p>
  <h1>{{ site.tagline }}</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Projects hold todos. A todo can wait on other todos, and one you are
    waiting on cannot be ticked off yet. Labels and due dates, and that is
    the app. A board and AI agents are there if you want them, and stay out
    of your way if you don't.
  </p>
  <p class="cta">
    <a class="button" href="{{ '/get-started/' | url }}">Get started</a>
    <a class="button secondary" href="{{ site.repo }}" rel="noopener">View on GitHub ↗</a>
  </p>

  <figure class="shot hero-shot">
    <div class="shot-frame">
      <picture>
        <source srcset="{{ '/assets/screenshots/todos-dark.webp' | url }}" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
        <img src="{{ '/assets/screenshots/todos.webp' | url }}" width="2560" height="1800" alt="A project in telos with AI off: todos with due dates, one overdue, labels, and a blocked todo naming the two it waits on." />
      </picture>
    </div>
    <figcaption>Telos with AI off: a project's todos, with due dates, labels and what is blocked.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Just todos</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    This is the whole app for a lot of people. A project opens as a list, and
    AI is off until you switch it on, so there is nothing to set up or turn
    off first.
  </p>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">✅</div>
      <h3>Type it, Enter, done</h3>
      <p>Add a todo in a sentence. Press <code>n</code> to add, <code>/</code> to filter, and <code>Ctrl K</code> to search every project.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🔗</div>
      <h3>What waits on what</h3>
      <p>A blocked todo sits in its own section with its blockers named and its checkbox disabled. Cycles are rejected when you try to make them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🏷️</div>
      <h3>Labels and due dates</h3>
      <p>Labels attach to projects and todos alike. A due date flags the todo when it is late, and a project can sort by them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Nice extras, when you want them</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    None of these are needed to use telos. Each is off, or simply unused,
    until you reach for it.
  </p>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🗂️</div>
      <h3>A board</h3>
      <p>The same todos as lanes you name yourself, one of which means done. Drag a card there and it is ticked off; tick the box and the card moves.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🤖</div>
      <h3>Agents on lanes</h3>
      <p>An agent is a model and its instructions. Put one on a lane and each todo there becomes a run that passes or fails and follows the lane's route.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🔌</div>
      <h3>Your own tools, over MCP</h3>
      <p>Point Claude Code or any MCP client at <code>/mcp</code> with an API key. Each key has a switch per tool, so a read-only key is one with its writing tools off.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="board-caption">
    AI is off on the instance, the account and the project until you switch it
    on, and a todo can say "AI ignores this". Set <code>AI_ENABLED=false</code>
    to remove it outright.
  </p>
</section>

